0..76 Comment "// A fold into the paths of a set respects its type\'s rules however its arms"
77..148 Comment "// compose those paths (#427). The integers, presented by successor and"
149..225 Comment "// predecessor with the two cancellations as rules, have no cells: two paths"
226..301 Comment "// between the same two integers are one path. So addition\'s commutativity,"
302..376 Comment "// whose arms run the recursive call through a lemma that nothing reduces,"
377..449 Comment "// meets each rule once its two sides\' endpoints convert, and the kernel"
450..525 Comment "// re-derives it. The circle\'s words, presented by the two cancellations of"
526..603 Comment "// the loop and its inverse, form a set the same way, so a path at every word"
604..679 Comment "// whose arms disagree on the nose agrees by its endpoints. A fold into the"
680..753 Comment "// circle\'s loops, which are no set\'s paths, is still held to its arms as"
754..765 Comment "// written."
767..812 Comment "/// The circle: one point and one loop at it."
